In the code editor, I realize that the container is an inline element, which might lead to long suggested text not wrapping properly. I think about using `white-space: pre-wrap` to maintain line breaks, but the text should wrap at spaces too. The tricky part is that in an inline-flex situation, the flex items—like text spans—might not wrap due to their default `min-width: auto`. So, I need to be careful and confirm that I set `min-width: 0` to prevent overflow.
