In my updated code, I’m using a try-catch block when resolving the adapter through `requireSourceAdapter(sourceId)`, which will allow me to handle errors more gracefully. If the adapter exists and has write capabilities, I'll proceed with my logic accordingly. I also need to ensure that `FileSourceAdapter` and `SourceCapability` types are imported at the top. Time to patch the function!
